  "caption": "Quinn bought a vibration plate, enjoyed ten minutes of effortless jiggling, and waited for abs. The abs stayed shy.\n\nVibration plates do switch muscles on a little, and the strongest evidence is for balance and function in frail older adults. Evidence for building bone, burning fat or shifting cellulite is weak, and shaky legs don't prove much.\n\nWhat can help: use a plate as a bridge if you can't load up yet, keep it as an add-on to walking, choose resistance training for leg strength, and get clearance first if you're pregnant or have a pacemaker, epilepsy, a recent fracture, joint replacement or clot history.\n\nGet checked promptly for new calf pain or swelling, chest pain, sudden vision change or dizziness.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
